# sandbox-devbox, read by sandbox-devbox.container via EnvironmentFile=.
#
# systemd env-file syntax: KEY=value, no quoting, `#` starts a comment.

# Where the devbox's secrets live: OpenBao (see sandbox/openbao/).
#
# There is no BAO_TOKEN here, and that is the fix rather than an omission: the
# root token used to be in this environment, where the agent could read it out
# and with it every secret in the sandbox. sshd-init now reads its own token —
# scoped to this container's one secret — from /vault/devbox.token, which
# sandbox/openbao/provision.sh mints at every boot.
BAO_ADDR=http://10.89.1.20:8200
VAULT_DIR=/vault

# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS and REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE are set by the image itself: the
# egress's proxy signs what it intercepts with the sandbox CA, which this image
# has in its trust store, but Node ships its own roots instead of reading it
# and Python's requests uses certifi. Both point at the system bundle, which
# holds the public roots plus the sandbox CA.
